      "hasMediaInOriginal": true,
      "fallbackReason": null,
      "text": "⚡️🇰🇵🇨🇳 North Korea & China pledges closer ties, calling for closer bilateral relationships and cooperation at a state-hosted banquet in Pyongyang, celebrating the 99th anniversary of the Chinese People's Liberation Army (PLA).\n\nThis is interpreted as a signal where Joseon-Sino relationship continues to thaw, as the two countries pledged to expand bilateral ties following the June summit.\n\nTraditionally, it has been celebrated through congratulatory messages or joint banquets, but this is one of the two unique occasions where by it is reported by Pyongyang's state media, with the last report dating to 2019.\n\nGeopolitical tensions have allowed North Korea to re-evaluate its standings in the international community & its relationship with China, placing the stability & continuation of the Kim dynasty to be at the number one priority.\n\nThe Sino-North Korean Treaty of Friendship, Cooperation and Mutual Assistance signed in 1961 remains the only formal mutual-defense pact where China is obligated to act, and will continue to go on. \n\n@medmannews",
